    <briefdescription>
<para>Byte-level half-duplex link between the UART and the node layer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The link owns the receive ring (filled from the UART interrupt), a parser with an inter-byte timeout and a transmitter that waits for a silent bus, checks the echo of its own bytes on a single-wire UART and detects a missing end of transmission. It reports what happened as events; the node layer (<ref refid="group__baton__node" kindref="compound">Node</ref>) uses it, applications normally do not call it directly.</para>
<para>The library never reads a clock: every function that needs the time takes <computeroutput>now_ms</computeroutput>, a monotonic millisecond counter that may wrap.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Public interface includes:</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Lifecycle: <ref refid="group__baton__link_1ga1ed6b9b13ba6070349988dad2f13d536" kindref="member">baton_link_init</ref>. </para>
</listitem>
